---
import EntryItem from "@/components/cv/EntryItem.astro";
import Section from "@/components/cv/Section.astro";
import SkillGroup from "@/components/cv/SkillGroup.astro";
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description: "Curriculum Vitae for Christopher Kennedy-Nuñez",
	title: "CV",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<div class="prose prose-sm">
		<h1>Christopher Kennedy-Nuñez</h1>
		<p class="cv-contact">
			Frontend Web Developer — Astoria, New York, US
			<br />Email: <a href="mailto:yo@furioursus.dev">yo@furioursus.dev</a>
			<br />Bluesky: <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/furioursus.dev">@furioursus.dev</a>
		</p>

		<Section title="Summary">
			<p>
				Front-end web developer with 14+ years of industry experience across web and print design,
				specializing in accessible HTML/CSS, WordPress, Craft CMS, and ExpressionEngine content
				management systems. A lifelong learner passionate about JavaScript, CSS, and HTML, driven to
				make the web — and the knowledge it carries — more accessible, and to leave the internet a
				better place. Believes in empowering the people around them to reach their goals through
				empathy and clear communication.
			</p>
		</Section>

		<Section title="Experience">
			<EntryItem
				title="Frontend Developer"
				subtitle="Fingerpaint Group"
				dates="Mar 2026–Present"
				url="https://fingerpaint.com"
			>
				Build pharmaceutical marketing websites using Astro and Vue. Leverage agentic LLM editors to
				build products such as dosing calculators and nurse/provider locators.
			</EntryItem>

			<EntryItem
				title="Front-End Web Developer & Owner"
				subtitle="One Bright Light / Furioursus"
				dates="2009–Present"
			>
				Design and develop websites using Craft CMS, ExpressionEngine, and e-commerce solutions,
				working with teams ranging from small 3-person startups to national agencies. Integrate
				third-party services to create more engaging website experiences, and heavily involved in
				developing information architecture for client sites, often acting as liaison between
				engineering and marketing teams.
			</EntryItem>

			<EntryItem
				title="Frontend Web Developer (Consultant, via Exygy)"
				subtitle="City of Oakland"
				dates="Feb 2022–Jul 2024"
				url="https://exygy.com"
			>
				Returned to the same oaklandca.gov project as an external consultant contracted through
				Exygy, continuing the modernization work from the earlier direct-employment tenure below.
			</EntryItem>

			<EntryItem
				title="Frontend Web Developer and Craft CMS Specialist (Business Analyst IV)"
				subtitle="City of Oakland"
				dates="Jul 2018–Feb 2021"
				url="https://oaklandca.gov"
			>
				Started as a contractor (Jul 2018–Feb 2019) before converting to staff as Business Analyst
				IV. Developed and maintained oaklandca.gov alongside a team of UX researchers and designers;
				civic tech work that emboldened a drive to serve the community.
				<Fragment slot="highlights">
					<li>
						Oversaw a Craft 2 to Craft 4 CMS conversion and migration, moving and retooling tens of
						thousands of entries that required content massaging mid-migration.
					</li>
					<li>
						Aggregated and analyzed staff feedback to build custom page content builders that
						maintained WCAG 2.0/2.1 compliance and preserved the City's brand guidelines; led staff
						training sessions and previewed upcoming technology to build staff buy-in.
					</li>
					<li>
						Served as point of contact for the City Administrator's office on accessibility
						requirements set by City Council; worked with external vendors contracted through other
						departments to ensure delivered code met compliance.
					</li>
					<li>Implemented a new realtime search tool, increasing on-site search traffic by 43%.</li>
					<li>
						Optimized web application performance with new caching guidelines after the start of the
						COVID-19 pandemic, increasing page speed 25-63%.
					</li>
					<li>
						Worked with the finance department to research, test, and implement third-party chatbot
						functionality, helping increase payment processing after city office closures.
					</li>
				</Fragment>
			</EntryItem>

			<EntryItem
				title="Craft and Frontend Web Developer"
				subtitle="Societyone"
				dates="Aug 2017–Mar 2018"
				url="https://societyone.com.au"
			>
				6-month contract with SocietyOne, a FinTech company in Australia, managing the project
				across a 17-hour timezone difference.
				<Fragment slot="highlights">
					<li>
						Maintained a large Craft CMS codebase and delivered new site features on quick
						turnaround for the marketing department.
					</li>
					<li>
						Integrated partner APIs for credit score information, increasing customer conversions by
						24%.
					</li>
					<li>
						Prototyped low-fidelity proofs of concept and implemented the design team's updates for
						production sites on tight deadlines.
					</li>
				</Fragment>
			</EntryItem>

			<EntryItem
				title="Front End Web Developer"
				subtitle="Blue State Digital"
				dates="Dec 2016–Mar 2017"
				url="https://bluestate.co"
			>
				3-month contract position working with BSD NYC and the City of New York.
				<Fragment slot="highlights">
					<li>
						Built AccessNYC (access.nyc.gov), an online tool helping New York City residents access
						food, money, housing, work, and other benefits/programs.
					</li>
					<li>Created the timeline and content structure for the CMS migration.</li>
					<li>
						Integrated the City's GatherContent headless CMS to sync and distribute content across
						the website and future systems.
					</li>
				</Fragment>
			</EntryItem>

			<EntryItem
				title="Lead Developer & Ad Campaign Manager"
				subtitle="Gaytravel"
				dates="May 2012–Oct 2014"
				url="https://gaytravel.com"
			>
				Maintained GayTravel.com's membership and content-driven website of over 10,000 users.
				Provided support and troubleshooting for the site, team, customers, and advertisers. Rebuilt
				the website from scratch with a cleaner design and implemented a responsive layout to meet
				the needs of a growing mobile user base.
			</EntryItem>

			<EntryItem
				title="Web Designer & ExpressionEngine Developer"
				subtitle="The Shotwell Company"
				dates="Nov 2010–Dec 2011"
				url="https://shotwellcompany.com"
			>
				Worked for a San Francisco-based web design and development studio building ExpressionEngine
				and Magento sites for nonprofits, NGOs, triple-bottom-line companies, and entrepreneurs,
				with clients including the United Nations, ShoreTel, BetterPlace.com, Cisco WebEx, the
				Cancer Prevention Institute of California, and the European Federation of Biotechnology.
			</EntryItem>

			<EntryItem
				title="Lead Designer"
				subtitle="Pwl Studio"
				dates="Jun 2007–Nov 2010"
				url="https://pwlstudio.com"
			>
				Houston-based full-service creative and marketing agency offering branding, web design and
				development, photography/video, and marketing automation across retail/luxury, energy,
				sports/media, nonprofit, and higher-education clients, including Tiffany & Co., Halliburton,
				ESPN, Neiman Marcus, the American Red Cross, and the University of Houston. Brought
				ExpressionEngine into the company's toolkit.
			</EntryItem>

			<EntryItem
				title="Graphic Designer"
				subtitle="copydotcom Inc"
				dates="May 2005–Jun 2007"
				url="https://copydotcom.com"
			>
				Served as web development liaison and managed and coordinated offset print orders, working
				with clients from conception to production across each stage.
			</EntryItem>

			<EntryItem
				title="Marketing Web Designer"
				subtitle="Adv Films"
				dates="2004–2005"
				url="https://advfilms.com"
				urlExpired
			>
				North American anime distribution and localization company (A.D. Vision). During this period
				ADV released titles including <em>Super Milk-chan</em> (July 2004-January 2005), <em
					>GetBackers</em
				> (August 2004-November 2005), and <em>Gantz</em> (2005), and ran the "Anime ADVocates" marketing
				program, which distributed free screening material and promotional content to nearly 3,000 anime
				clubs across North America.
			</EntryItem>

			<EntryItem
				title="Web & Graphic Designer"
				subtitle="iTechLabs"
				dates="Jan 2003–Jul 2004"
				url="https://itechlabs.com"
				urlExpired
			>
				First web-related job; in charge of developing interactive websites.
			</EntryItem>
		</Section>

		<Section title="Education">
			<EntryItem
				boldSubtitle={false}
				title="Associate of Arts and Sciences (AAS), Multimedia & Web Design"
				subtitle="Art Institute of Houston"
				dates="Jan 2001–Jan 2004"
			/>
		</Section>

		<Section title="Skills">
			<SkillGroup
				label="Technical"
				items={[
					"3rd Party Integrations",
					"Accessibility",
					"Agentic Development",
					"APIs",
					"Astro",
					"Content Management Systems (CMS)",
					"Craft CMS",
					"CSS",
					"Drupal",
					"ExpressionEngine",
					"Front-end Development",
					"Git",
					"Google Analytics",
					"HAML",
					"HTML",
					"Information Architecture",
					"JavaScript",
					"PHP",
					"SASS",
					"User Experience",
					"Vue.js",
					"Web Development",
					"Web Standards",
					"WordPress",
					"XML",
				]}
			/>
			<SkillGroup
				label="Creative"
				items={[
					"Adobe Creative Suite",
					"Graphic Design",
					"Illustrator",
					"InDesign",
					"Photoshop",
					"User Interface Design",
					"Web Design",
				]}
			/>
		</Section>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
